<section class="case-lenses"><p class="eyebrow">CONNECTING THE PERSPECTIVES</p><h2>Experience.<br/>Operations.<br/>Strategy.</h2><div><details class="lens-detail"><summary><span>01</span>Experience<b aria-hidden="true">＋</b></summary><p>Value proposition work considered the needs of Braskem and prospective external customers.</p></details><details class="lens-detail"><summary><span>02</span>Operations<b aria-hidden="true">＋</b></summary><p>Ownership mapping exposed responsibilities, dependencies and gaps across areas.</p></details><details class="lens-detail"><summary><span>03</span>Strategy<b aria-hidden="true">＋</b></summary><p>SWOT, uncertainty mapping and prioritisation connected the existing operation with future growth questions.</p></details></div></section>
<section class="outcomes" id="outcomes"><p class="eyebrow">OUTPUTS &amp; OUTCOMES</p><h2>What the work made possible.</h2><p>The workshop produced ownership and roadblock maps, value proposition work, strategic analysis and a prioritised set of opportunities. Its contribution was an early foundation for leadership and team alignment; subsequent commercial growth is not quantified in this case.</p><div class="reflection"><h3>What I take forward</h3><p>The workshop was a means to an organisational conversation. The larger design challenge was how a new business would coordinate its areas and relationships as its service offer evolved.</p></div></section></div><a class="next-case" href={withBase('work/go-to-market/')}><div><p class="eyebrow">NEXT CASE / 05</p><h2>From a broad prospect list to clearer customer fit.</h2></div><span aria-hidden="true" class="round-arrow">↗</span></a></main>
